title: 'Missing error: reading a virtual property inside its own accessor'
updated_at: "2026-11-05T09:32:09Z"
---
Openplanet (TM2020 in-game compile) rejects reading a virtual property inside its own accessor with "No matching symbol", but openplanet-lsp reports no error.

Repro (Dips++ Editor, branch fix/honest-dirty-tracking @96386fb, Floors.as:140, 2026-10-19):
```
float get_px_lastFloorEnd() { return _px_lastFloorEnd; }
void set_px_lastFloorEnd(float v) {
    if (px_lastFloorEnd != v) MarkDirty();   // Openplanet: No matching symbol `px_lastFloorEnd`
    _px_lastFloorEnd = v;
}
```
Expected: LSP emits an error like the game compiler (or at least a warning) when the property name is used inside its own get_/set_ accessor. Workaround: call get_px_lastFloorEnd() explicitly.

Related: #73 (LSP misses ++/--/+= on properties). Both are property-accessor semantics the LSP does not model; worth fixing together.